Devops cmd 

-----------------------GIT -------------------

| Command                   | What it does                                   | Small difference                                 |
| ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |
| `git clone <URL>`         | Downloads a repo for the first time            | Creates a **new local copy**                     |
| `git status`              | Shows current changes/state                    | **Only checks**, doesn't change anything         |
| `git branch`              | Shows local branches                           | Tells you which branch you're on                 |
| `git switch main`         | Switches branch                                | Moves between branches                           |
| `git pull origin main`    | Gets latest changes from Azure and merges them | **Download + merge**                             |
| `git fetch origin`        | Gets latest information from Azure             | **Download only**, doesn't merge                 |
| `git diff`                | Shows changes in modified files                | Compares **working files vs local commit**       |
| `git diff origin/main`    | Compares local files with remote branch        | Shows differences against Azure's `main`         |
| `git add .`               | Stages changes                                 | Prepares changes for commit                      |
| `git restore --staged .`  | Unstages changes                               | Removes changes from staging, keeps file changes |
| `git restore .`           | Discards local unstaged changes                | Restores files to last local commit              |
| `git commit -m "message"` | Creates a local commit                         | Saves changes **locally**                        |
| `git push origin main`    | Uploads commits to Azure                       | **Local → Azure**                                |
| `git log --oneline`       | Shows commit history                           | View previous commits                            |
| `git revert HEAD`         | Creates a commit that reverses last commit     | Safely **undoes a pushed commit**                |
| `git reset --hard HEAD~1` | Removes last local commit and changes          | Dangerous if already pushed                      |
| `git remote -v`           | Shows Azure Repo URL                           | Checks where `origin` points                     |
